{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:07:49.158978Z","id":"370cdcd3887110f51895282eee93acc893f02cf7243eb67dde321aa956824b5a","body":{"detail":"Embed::open starts the core with require_credential: true (spec §2.3), and a shell-page frame carries no credential (spec §2.3 table; crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs request() drops authorization and cookie for it). clax_http::auth::require_credential (crates/clax-http/src/auth.rs:347-363) lets through only open_without_credential's paths (/healthz, /_clax/, /c/, /_blob/; auth.rs:332-337), so GET /a/<id>?app=1 and /assets/... as shell-page answer 401 unauthorized. Probed through Embed::call on a fresh home: '/a/<id>?app=1 -> 401 {\"error\":{\"code\":\"unauthorized\",...}}', '/_clax/bridge.js -> 200', '/c/<id>/v/1/ -> 200'. The daemon app avoided this with the clax_key_<port> cookie, which also made the shell document's boot data the owner's (shell/boot.rs assemble: who.is_owner()). Options: (a) the core adds the owner's credential to shell-page frames, since the host sends them only for the shell origin's main-frame navigation and its subresources (spec §4.2), keeping today's owner boot data; (b) open_without_credential admits /a/, /assets/ and /favicon.ico when AppState.embed is set, and the shell document's boot is a visitor's until the shell fetches over ClaxHost; (c) the core runs without require_credential, as nothing but the app can reach it (spec §4.3, no port). Phase 1's tests do not load the shell document; Tasks 14 and 15 (the scheme handlers and the host relay) need one of these.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":368},"end":{"line":373},"content_hash":"4dd88cffd385f2ccccb1be4ffa321d6c52b08921f2ac3b9e0586670160aa9616"},"summary":"A shell-page frame for the shell document or its assets answers 401 under the core's require_credential, so the app's WebView cannot load the shell as spec 2026-10-19 §2.3 frames it","tags":["status:needs-decision","embed","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:24:57.700310Z","id":"353a5bfe8ab3936b81f89d5a19b076c84ec473e51cd0908ef623dac33f2f91fb","body":{"detail":"ffi_open passes OpenOptions.log: None, since clax_embed_open (include/clax_embed.h) takes only the home, and spec 2026-10-19 §2.1 lists src/log.rs (the rolling log moved from clax-ios, which logged to <cache>/daemon.log) without saying where its path comes from. The app's core therefore logs nowhere. A path in <home>/embed.json beside the origins, or a fixed <home>/logs/core.log, would need the spec to say which.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"9d27fbc89fbf57016f3423d76cc5d0a2b41e8c1d537a59a2fdc934be680fb49d"},"summary":"A core opened through clax_embed_open writes no log: the C ABI names no log path","tags":["embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
